# Line endings are part of the product claim: same (source, packs, theme, tool
# version) → byte-identical SVG, LF always. Without this file, Git for Windows'
# default core.autocrlf=true checks every tracked text file out as CRLF — 918 of
# them, measured — and then the goldens byte-compare an LF render against a CRLF
# file, `render --check` calls every committed diagram stale, the ```squinch
# fence regexes in skill.test.ts / readme.test.ts match nothing, and
# sync-examples inlines \r\n into examples.ts so CI's `git diff --exit-code`
# fails. A Windows clone and a macOS clone must have identical bytes on disk.

# `eol=lf` is the load-bearing half. Bare `text=auto` normalizes on commit but
# still smudges to CRLF on a Windows checkout, and the working tree is what
# readFileSync sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The source format and the artifact, said out loud — redundant with the rule
# above, and here so that grepping this file answers "what happens to a
# .squinch" without knowing how text=auto's content heuristic works.
*.squinch text eol=lf
*.svg     text eol=lf

# Scripts git runs through sh. A CR before the newline is a syntax error
# (`\r: command not found`) that reads as the hook being broken rather than the
# checkout being wrong.
.githooks/*        text eol=lf
packages/cli/bin/* text eol=lf

# Binaries, declared rather than detected. text=auto's heuristic (NUL in the
# first 8000 bytes) happens to get all eleven of these right today, but nobody
# decided that — `git ls-files --eol` shows them as -text with an empty attr
# column. Saying it means a future asset that looks textual to the heuristic
# cannot be silently mangled.
*.ttf   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.vsix  binary

# Pack icons ship VERBATIM — the AWS set is licensed no-derivatives (NOTICE),
# and the bytes are a render input, so "identical on every platform" becomes a
# git attribute rather than a hope. `-text` also stops `git add --renormalize`
# from rewriting packages/pack-azure/icons/translator-text.svg, the one tracked
# file that arrives from upstream with a CRLF terminator. Note this does not
# make the diffs binary (that would be -diff); icon diffs stay readable.
packages/pack-*/icons/** -text
